<threat_model>
## Trust Boundaries

| Boundary | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| HTTP API → service layer | Authenticated requests from tenant admins. Tenant isolation enforced by _tid() helper — all DB queries filter by tenant_id unless role == super_admin. |
| Service layer → email delivery | Outbound SMTP. Recipient addresses come from tenant-supplied schedule data. |
| Service layer → filesystem | _generate_pdf() writes to static/reports/. Ephemeral files deleted after attach. |
| Background scheduler → MongoDB | Unattended loop reads report_schedules. No external input surface; only attacks via previously-stored schedule documents. |

## STRIDE Threat Register

| Threat ID | Category | Component | Disposition | Mitigation Plan |
|-----------|----------|-----------|-------------|-----------------|
| T-10-01 | Spoofing | GET /history endpoint | mitigate | Existing get_current_user JWT dependency enforces identity; _tid() raises 403 if tenant context absent |
| T-10-02 | Tampering | framework_id field in create payload | mitigate | framework_id is a plain string passed to _generate_pdf(); the PDF generator calls db.compliance_frameworks find — if framework_id does not exist, it returns empty data (not an error path). No shell execution or path construction from framework_id. |
| T-10-03 | Information Disclosure | GET /history cross-tenant | mitigate | get_delivery_history filters by tenant_id when role != super_admin; super_admin access is role-checked by existing auth middleware |
| T-10-04 | Denial of Service | scheduler loop generating unbounded PDFs | mitigate | Due-schedules query has to_list(length=50) cap; ephemeral PDF deleted after each send so disk does not fill |
| T-10-05 | Elevation of Privilege | SMTP config validation bypass | accept | SMTP config is platform-level (not per-tenant); check is a soft guard to prevent useless schedule creation — not a security boundary |
| T-10-06 | Information Disclosure | PDF temporary file readable by other tenants | mitigate | File is deleted immediately after bytes read; static/reports/ is not publicly browsable (download endpoint enforces tenant check) |
| T-10-SC | Tampering | npm/pip/cargo installs | accept | No new packages installed in this plan — stdlib + already-present reportlab and email_service only |
</threat_model>

